# Every subdirectory here is its own git repository -- plus target/, scratch/
# and editor state. Tracking any of them would embed a repo inside this one,
# which is the hazard behind the old "do not git init here" rule. Ignoring all
# subdirectories by glob rather than by name means adding a crate needs no edit
# here, and a new crate can never be swallowed by accident.
/*/

# ...except the workspace's own cargo config, which is part of what this repo
# exists to version.
!/.cargo/
